{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaDirectionSanityGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaDirectionSanityGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.direction_sanity_threshold_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.direction_sanity_threshold_positive","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L109-L115","doc":"**Threshold positivity**: 10 > 0. Used downstream when reasoning\nabout the threshold's role as a tolerance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.direction_sanity_gate_reject","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.direction_sanity_gate_reject","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L93-L107","doc":"**The gate theorem (refute direction): rejection lemma.**\n\nIf a candidate predicts a magnitude `m` whose distance from the\ntarget exceeds the threshold, then the gate class cannot be\ninstantiated for that magnitude — the candidate is structurally\nREFUTED. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.qbeta_direction_sanity_magnitude_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.qbeta_direction_sanity_magnitude_match","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**The gate theorem (forward direction): under the class, the\ncandidate's magnitude matches the target within threshold.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:q-beta-direction-sanity-gate","label":"rem:q-beta-direction-sanity-gate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass.magnitude_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass.magnitude_match","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Structural identity: the candidate's magnitude at q_0 matches\nthe target within the 10× threshold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.DirectionSanityGateClass","kind":"class","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L66-L82","doc":"**Direction-sanity gate class (§3b-cond, PARAMETRIC).**\n\nParametric over the candidate's substrate magnitude `m_candidate`\n(per Gemini high-priority review on PR #1890): allows multiple\ncandidates to be checked in the same environment by instantiating\nthe class with each candidate's predicted F(q_0) magnitude.\n\nAxiomatises the structural prediction that the candidate's\nmagnitude at q_0 is within the 10× threshold of the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.directionSanityThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.directionSanityThreshold","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**The 10× order-of-magnitude direction-sanity threshold.**\n\nSet deliberately loose: catches order-of-magnitude direction\nerrors (like PR #1850's z < 1 vs target > 1) without false-\npositives on the small numerical deviations covered by the\n§4(a) radius-of-convergence and §4(c) q=1 shadow gates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.qBetaTargetMagnitudeAtQ0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DirectionSanityGate.qBetaTargetMagnitudeAtQ0","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-direction-sanity-gate.lean#L48-L55","doc":"**The substrate target magnitude.**\n\n`Q_β^CODATA / (Q_A(q_0) · cos(α_eff(q_0))) ≈ 0.99824` at the\nproton-pinned q_0; the precision-ladder product\n`∏_k(1 + c_k u^k)` collectively contributes only ~0.18% of the\nbare `Q_A · cos` value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}